    content_en: `<h2>The Spiritual Significance of the Aarti</h2>
            <p>Attending the daily Aartis of Maa Vindhyavasini is considered a blessing. The word 'Aarti' is derived from the Sanskrit word 'Aratrika', meaning that which removes darkness. The rhythmic sound of bells, conch shells (shankhnaad), and the chanting of stotrams during the Aarti create a highly charged spiritual atmosphere that purifies the mind of negative energies.</p>
            <h3>Official Aarti Lyrics (Hindi Devanagari)</h3>
            <p>Here is the traditional Aarti sung daily during the Shringar:</p>
            <blockquote>
                <em>सुनो सुनो हे विन्ध्यवासिनी माता, तुम हो दुःख दारिद्र्य की नाशक।<br/>
                संत जनों के काज सँवारो, जय भवानी हे जगपालक॥<br/>
                महिषासुर मर्दिनी जय दुर्गे, भक्तों के संकट हरने वाली।<br/>
                चन्द्रकला मस्तक पर सोहे, अष्टभुजी मैया मतवाली॥<br/>
                सिंहवाहिनी मैया मेरी, कंचन थाल आरती साजूँ।<br/>
                धूप दीप नैवेद्य चढ़ा कर, शंख मृदंग की ध्वनि बाजूँ॥<br/>
                जय जय विन्ध्याचल की रानी, कृपा करो हे आदि भवानी।<br/>
                जो कोई तुम्हारी आरती गावे, सो सब सुख सम्पत्ति पावे॥</em>
            </blockquote>
            <h3>English Transliteration of the Verse</h3>
            <p>Devotees who wish to sing along can refer to this transliteration:</p>
            <p><em>"Suno Suno He Vindhyavasini Mata, Tum Ho Dukh Daridrya Ki Nashak.<br/>
            Sant Janon Ke Kaaj Sanwaro, Jai Bhavani He Jagpalak.<br/>
            Mahishasur Mardini Jai Durge, Bhakton Ke Sankat Harne Wali.<br/>
            Chandrakala Mastak Par Sohe, Ashtabhuji Maiya Matwali..."</em></p>
            <h3>How to Perform Aarti at Home</h3>
            <p>To perform the Aarti at home, light a brass lamp with ghee or camphor (kapur). Face the North or East direction. Move the lamp in a gentle circular motion clockwise around the image of Maa Vindhyavasini. Offer red flowers and sweets as bhog after completion.</p>`,
